@* Own-ship indicator toggles. Master gate for the lines drawn around
   the boat icon that are info / prediction (not navigation guidance):
     * COG vector + tip dot + "10 min / N nm" label
     * Tidal current arrow (drift direction)
     * Laylines (port + stbd, when sailing)

   Bearing line + XTE tick are intentionally NOT in this group --
   they're navigation guidance, only show when a route is active, and
   hiding them mid-leg would be a foot-gun.

   Local trail toggle lives here too so all "own-ship-on-the-chart"
   knobs are in one place. Server history stays in its own section
   below since it's a different data source with its own duration /
   resolution dropdowns. *@

<SectionHeader Title="Own ship"
               Expanded="@expanded"
               OnToggle="() => expanded = !expanded" />
@if (expanded)
{
    <label class="chart-item">
        <input type="checkbox" checked="@ShipLinesVisible"
               @onchange="(e) => OnToggleShipLines.InvokeAsync((bool)(e.Value ?? false))" />
        <div class="chart-item-body">
            <div class="chart-name">Show ship lines</div>
            <div class="chart-desc">COG vector, tidal current, laylines</div>
        </div>
    </label>
}

@code {
    [Parameter] public bool ShipLinesVisible { get; set; } = true;
    [Parameter] public EventCallback<bool> OnToggleShipLines { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Default expanded so a fresh helm sees the toggles
    /// without hunting; collapsing is one tap. The Own ship section
    /// is shorter than e.g. Charts so default-expanded doesn't bloat
    /// the panel.</summary>
    private bool expanded = true;
}
